<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Responsive Layout Demo</title>
    <style>
        
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            font-family: sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            
            padding: 2vw; 
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        
        .header-section {
            background-color: #2c3e50;
            color: white;
            padding: 2rem;
            text-align: center;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

    
        .highlight-text {
            color: #f1c40f;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        
        .main-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column; 
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .card {
            
            width: 100%; 
            background: #ecf0f1;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            border: 1px solid #bdc3c7;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }

    
        
        @media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
            .main-container {
                flex-direction: row; 
            }

            .card {
                
                flex: 1; 
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="header-section">
        <h1>Welcome to My <span class="highlight-text">Responsive</span> Page</h1>
        <p>This layout adapts based on your screen size.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="main-container">
        <div class="card">
            <h3>Column 1</h3>
            <p>On mobile, this card takes up <span class="highlight-text">100% width</span>. On desktop, it sits side-by-side with others.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h3>Column 2</h3>
            <p>We use <strong>media queries</strong> to detect the browser width and update the CSS flex-direction.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
